meta {
  name: Create Faq
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/faqs
  body: json
  auth: basic
}

auth:basic {
  username: {{admin_username}}
  password: {{admin_password}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/ld+json
}

body:json {
  {
    "question": "Combien de jours de congés par an ?",
    "answer": "25 jours ouvrés, proratisés la première année."
  }
}

docs {
  Added 2026-09-02: Faq gained a `Post` operation (ROLE_ADMIN), so creation
  is no longer backoffice-only -- unlike AiAgent, which still has no writable
  API operation at all. Edition/deletion are still not exposed here: no
  `Put`/`Patch`/`Delete` on this resource, only `/admin/faqs` (session +
  CSRF) can change or remove an existing FAQ. See Update/Delete Category for
  what that would look like if it existed.

  No validation constraints on the entity beyond the two required fields
  (`question`, `answer` -- see FaqType); `category` (IRI, e.g.
  `/api/document_categories/{id}`), `tags` (array of strings), `priority`
  (int) and `isHighlighted`/`isActive` (bool) are all optional and default
  to `0`/`[]`/`false`/`true` respectively. Verified via curl against a
  running container: 201 with just `question`+`answer`, defaults applied as
  above; a follow-up `PATCH`/`DELETE` on the created id both return 405.
}
